  "_meta": {
    "pack": "derm-education",
    "purpose": "The sources the dermatology and skincare education pack (content/derm/articles) is written from. Every entry was opened on the accessed date and read; the dates are the ones the page itself showed. Nothing here was invented or guessed: a page that could not be opened is not listed.",
    "checked_on": "2026-10-21",
    "checked_by": "AI-assisted software draft (Claude). Not a clinician. A qualified clinician must still confirm the wording of every article before it is treated as approved.",
    "how_the_text_is_written": "All wording in the articles is original (short plain-language statements written for patients). The sources are summarised, never copied, and every article names the sources it rests on. No images are used.",
    "terms_bases": {
      "ogl_v3": "NHS website content is released under the Open Government Licence v3.0 (https://www.nhs.uk/our-policies/terms-and-conditions/, read 2026-10-21). Adapted wording must not be presented as the NHS's own text; the required notice is: 'Contains public sector information licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0.'",
      "us_gov_public_domain": "A work of the US federal government (MedlinePlus health-topic pages, NIH, CDC, FDA pages): generally not copyrighted. MedlinePlus asks for the credit 'Source: MedlinePlus, National Library of Medicine' (https://medlineplus.gov/about/using/usingcontent/, read 2026-10-21). Page-level notices were checked; third-party images are never used.",
      "restricted_facts_only": "Copyrighted website. Its terms (https://www.aad.org/terms-use, summarised from a search result 2026-10-21; the page itself was not opened) forbid reproducing or ingesting its content without written permission. So NO wording is taken from it: the pack states widely-held facts in original words, with a link for the reader, and every such statement is also listed for the clinic's own review. If the clinic wants closer wording it must ask the owner for permission (permissions@aad.org) and have its counsel confirm."
    }
  },
